{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784572724,"nonce":"SulKzYzgK2bo81V/abL5FwPT7OM=","title":"Implements ADR-0057 (`docs/adr/0057-run-provenance-trigger-context.md`) — the foundational tracer bullet. Reference the ADR for the locked decisions and the security boundary.","message":"The push commit-subject **headline** (CONTEXT.md \"Headline / trigger title\"), end-to-end: a `push`-triggered run stamps the head-commit **subject** into a new `runs.trigger_title`, exposes it on both read DTOs, and renders it as the secondary line of a single shared **Trigger-cell** UI component reused by the runs list and the run-detail top context bar.\n\nThis slice also lays the plumbing every later slice reuses: the `trigger_title` column, the `trigger_title(event)` extractor + stamp point, the `Event` enrichment pattern, and the shared UI component.\n\n- Migration `0032_run_trigger_title.sql` — nullable `runs.trigger_title TEXT` (no backfill; pre-migration runs show no headline, like origin/pipeline).\n- `Event::Push` gains `message: String`; both adapters (`scarab-forge-github`, `scarab-forge-forgejo`) parse `head_commit.message`; extend each adapter's existing payload fixtures to carry a message.\n- **Security boundary (load-bearing):** the new field must NOT enter `Event::context()` (the CEL/`${{ }}` map). Add a code comment at `context()` stating provenance fields are excluded. See ADR-0057 Q6/Q7.\n- A `trigger_title(event) -\u003e Option\u003cString\u003e` extractor: for `push`, the commit **subject** (first line only), truncated server-side to **200 chars** on a char boundary, stored clean (no ellipsis). Stamped in `persist_run_from_ir` beside `set_run_origin`/`set_run_pipeline` (new `set_run_trigger_title`/`run_trigger_title` ports in db-postgres + testkit).\n- `RunSummaryDto` and `RunStatusResponse` gain `trigger_title: Option\u003cString\u003e`; threaded onto both `list_runs*` SELECTs and `get_run`. Regenerate OpenAPI + UI schema.\n- One shared **Trigger-cell component** in the web UI, reused by `RepoView` (runs list) and `RunDetail` (top context bar) — replacing the currently-duplicated JSX (they share `trigger.ts` helpers today). Renders trigger kind on top, headline as the truncated secondary line with a full-text tooltip.\n\n\n- [ ] Migration applies on real PG; a fresh push run persists `trigger_title` = commit subject (verified via `GET /v1/runs/{id}` and the runs list DTO).\n- [ ] Commit subject only (body dropped), truncated to 200 chars on a char boundary, no ellipsis in the stored value.\n- [ ] `Event::context()` does NOT expose `message`; a test asserts the provenance field is absent from the context map; the code comment is present.\n- [ ] Both GitHub and Forgejo adapter payload tests parse the message from a fixture.\n- [ ] The Trigger cell is a single component rendered identically in the runs list and the run-detail context bar; a push run shows `push` + the subject beneath.\n- [ ] Pre-migration / null-headline runs degrade gracefully (no headline line, no crash).\n- [ ] `just check` + targeted `cargo test` green; OpenAPI regenerated and committed.\n\n\nNone - can start immediately.","files":null}]}